  "details": {
    "2c5cba07e3c30fc1d80788ef57c4bf6a6731261c": {
      "message": "chore(site): align the portal with dsh-git 0.5.0\n\nThe portal still advertised four dsh-git agent tools (removed in 0.3.0),\nsix tools in total, the removed `tools` and `defaultWorkspaceId` config\nkeys, and \"no merge, rebase, cherry-pick\" limits. It never mentioned the\ncomposer branch chip or worktree management, and the dsh-git page kept a\nsecond hardcoded copy of the feature list beside the one in plugins.ts —\nwhich is why the two drifted.\n\nRender `plugin.features` instead of a local copy, drop the git tools\nsection, and show a tools count only where a plugin has tools. Install\ncommands, the DSH requirement and the header version now come from\nplugins-meta.json, so a version bump cannot leave copy behind again.\n\nBoundaries now describe what the API actually accepts (a snapshot read\nmay name the Session directory; mutations may not), and limits list what\nthe panel really does: no stash, no conflict resolution, rebase flattens\nmerges, drop refuses a range containing them.",
      "author": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "litingyes",
        "email": "luz.liting@gmail.com"
      },
      "committedAt": "2026-11-07T00:34:32+08:00",
      "files": [
