    "8737129fbc999197a83288d90a0c8278ccb0cbf3": {
      "message": "feat(git): act on commits and branches from the panel\n\nRight-click a commit node for copy SHA, cherry-pick, revert, and drop;\ndropping removes that one commit from the current branch and replays its\ndescendants onto its parent. Right-click a branch row to merge it into the\ncurrent branch or rebase the current branch onto it; local and remote\nbranches are both targets.\n\nThe Host gained five history actions on the existing action route. Each\nrequires an attached HEAD, no stopped operation, and a clean tracked\nworktree, and a conflict runs the matching `--abort` before returning a\nstructured code, so the repository is never left half-way. Drop needs\n`confirm: true` and refuses a root or merge commit, a commit outside the\ncurrent branch, and a rewrite range that contains merges. `state` now\nreports the in-progress operation, so both tabs can disable an entry and\nsay why instead of failing after the click.\n\nEvery panel action that used a text label is now an icon button with a\nhost-styled tooltip that also carries the disabled reason; the commit CTA,\nmodal dialog buttons, and the graph's mode toggle keep their labels.\nTooltips and context menus use the host menu material, and the new pure\n`commit-actions` / `branch-actions` modules keep the availability rules\ntestable without a DOM.\n\nDocument the new actions and limits, update the locale metadata, and bump\nthe package to 0.5.0 with a rebuilt client.js.",
